m i mean you played third base and  you were a catcher you you how's the  hose can you can you still get it there  well i had all rotator cuffs into  surgery since then which should make it  better but uh i may be able to throw it  damn but i'm not sure exactly what  direction  didn't you once what was the batting  average 363  363 yes  and you and you weren't exactly  you know fast  like no i i i didn't get many of those  hits right  it was it was a magical year don't ask  me but it was  it was a special time and  [Music]  363 though i mean yeah i had 230 hits it  was crazy it was crazy  i also have you for 23 stolen bases in  18 seasons  not bad  uh you know i tried to i tried to steal  once in every part of the country this  way it would be a shock  to i remember tom seaver tom seaver was  on the mound one night and and i'm gonna  you know and the only time i would try  to steal was like if it was two strikes  on the hitter you know and stuff like  that where he'd get a free count next  inning  and tom sieber would always come to a  you know a set position and look over to  first base and then with pitch  so  he did that and he looked over to first  base and when he went back to  you know looked toward home i took off  and then he looked back over there and  he still threw home figuring i'm not  going to make it anyway  yeah but that yeah i uh 23 stolen bases  that may have been inflated but see what  happens uh thanks again for reminiscing  and uh have fun with bobby valentine  tomorrow and this weekend joe it's  always great to talk to you  thanks dan same here that's joe torre  hall of famer and uh major league  baseball special assistant to the  commissioner it'll be the yankees and  mets at citi field tomorrow night bobby  valentine who was the mets manager back  uh  you know following 911 and uh joe torre  the ceremonial first pitches


